content:
All four failing orders are from the same supplier (Al-Noor Trading) and all created at t=660, exactly when the worker deploy landed. This is ambiguous: it could be the worker deploy broke parsing of this supplier's format, OR Al-Noor Trading started sending a new layout at t=660. I need to check whether orders from Al-Noor Trading were processed successfully before t=660 (which would point to bad_deploy) or if this supplier is entirely new (which would point to bad_input).

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT o.id, o.supplier, o.created_at, m.attempts, m.state FROM orders o LEFT JOIN messages m ON m.order_id = o.id WHERE o.supplier = 'Al-Noor Trading' ORDER BY o.created_at ASC LIMIT 20",
      "why": "Check if Al-Noor Trading had successfully processed orders before t=660. If yes, the worker deploy broke parsing of a known format (bad_deploy). If all Al-Noor orders start at t=660, it may be a new supplier with an unsupported layout (bad_input)."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [],
  "summary": "Investigating whether Al-Noor Trading invoices were successfully processed before t=660 to distinguish a worker deploy regression from a new bad-input supplier format."
}
```
